The module map gains the chat_chain.py row: the chat generation chain
helpers (archive order, cursor-generation resolution, the A2A-free row
stream, immutable source retention) moved out of consolidator.py into their
own D15 module, and the same row then names the index-free chat row
addresses (row:<chat_id>@<ts>#<sha12>, resolved by hint, then by the archive
rotated after the row's ts) and the stream positions shared with the legacy
cursor. The chronicle_store.py row follows it: the append-only derived
memory journal with its disposable SQLite index, pages sealing row sets once,
parts folding adjacent records once, room-head checks and typed refusals.
The chronicle_import.py row names the one model-free import of the legacy
dialogue memory: a legacy record per room section with its positional
raw_range, nominations as global marks, the legacy_frontier scan state and
the activation receipt. The tools/ section gains the chronicle.py row: the
three memory tools (chronicle_write, memory_read, memory_mark) exported
through knowledge.py, with host-expanded page row sets, task stamps, checked
quotes and reads paged at the source. Retiring the old dialogue writer removes
the room_consolidation.py row, rewrites the consolidator.py row (the shared
Light transport and scratchpad/knowledge upkeep) and the
memory_nomination_receipts.py row (strict read of the frozen cursor's
nominations), marks dialogue_blocks.json and dialogue_meta.json in the data
layout as frozen legacy read once by the import, and adds the chronicle/ row
(records.jsonl, index.sqlite3, .publication.lock). Later steps of the same
memory change update this first line to the chapter's net growth since
1347e33bf.
